--- !u!1001 &4333744620142798585
PrefabInstance:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  serializedVersion: 2
  m_Modification:
    serializedVersion: 3
    m_TransformParent: {fileID: 4057622884236373629}
    m_Modifications:
    - target: {fileID: 4882262320171367339, guid: c480ee079c800aa42a2a66683d2783ad, type: 3}
      propertyPath: m_text
      value: "Roman Terracotta Oil Lamp with Cupid\n\nTerracotta oil lamp from the
        Early Roman Empire (1st century BCE\u20131st century CE), measuring 9.9 cm
        long. Used in homes and public spaces for everyday lighting. Its simple,
        practical form reflects Roman ceramic design. From the Cesnola Collection,
        now in The Met.\n\nBird Woman\n\nTerracotta figurine from Predynastic Egypt
        (Naqada II, c. 3500\u20133400 BCE). With outstretched arms and a birdlike
        shape, it highlights feminine features linked to fertility. Likely used in
        ritual or burial, symbolising transformation, rebirth, or spiritual power.\n\nBaby
        Feeding Animal Vessel\n\nReplica of Bronze and Iron Age vessels from Central
        Europe, made of smoke-fired terracotta. Animal-shaped with a spout, it resembles
        a feeding bottle. Traces of milk show use in infant care, possibly easing
        weaning. Combines function with creative, calming design."
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 4882262320171367339, guid: c480ee079c800aa42a2a66683d2783ad, type: 3}
      propertyPath: m_fontSize
      value: 4.7
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 4882262320171367339, guid: c480ee079c800aa42a2a66683d2783ad, type: 3}
