--- !u!1001 &4468706473681291531
PrefabInstance:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  serializedVersion: 2
  m_Modification:
    serializedVersion: 3
    m_TransformParent: {fileID: 4057622884236373629}
    m_Modifications:
    - target: {fileID: 4882262320171367339, guid: c480ee079c800aa42a2a66683d2783ad, type: 3}
      propertyPath: m_text
      value: "Roman Votive Foot\n\nReplica of a Roman anatomical offering left at
        healing sanctuaries for ailments of the foot. Often dedicated to Asclepius,
        these votives symbolised prayer or thanks. Common across the Roman world,
        they reflect belief in divine healing through body-focused ritual.\n\nBout
        Coup\xE9 Handaxe\n\nFlint handaxe made by Neanderthals in Britain around
        60,000\u201340,000 years ago. Named for its rounded base and triangular shape,
        it was finely flaked for cutting tasks. Unique to Britain, it shows local
        adaptation and late Neanderthal craftsmanship.\n\nMinoan Snake Goddess\n\nBronze
        Age figure from Knossos, Crete, dated to c. 1600 BCE. Made of faience, she
        holds snakes and may wear a feline crown. Possibly a goddess or priestess,
        she symbolises fertility, renewal, and chthonic power in Minoan ritual and
        belief."
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 4882262320171367339, guid: c480ee079c800aa42a2a66683d2783ad, type: 3}
      propertyPath: m_fontSize
