--- !u!1001 &5054970393346618977
PrefabInstance:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  serializedVersion: 2
  m_Modification:
    serializedVersion: 3
    m_TransformParent: {fileID: 4057622884236373629}
    m_Modifications:
    - target: {fileID: 4882262320171367339, guid: c480ee079c800aa42a2a66683d2783ad, type: 3}
      propertyPath: m_text
      value: 'Roman Votive Hand


        Replica of a terracotta votive hand from
        the British Museum. Such offerings were left at healing sanctuaries across
        the Greco-Roman world, often dedicated to gods like Asclepius. They reflect
        beliefs in divine healing and the connection between religion and medicine.


        Bronze
        Flanged Axe


        Early Bronze Age axe from Britain marking the move
        from stone to metal. Raised flanges secured the blade to a wooden handle.
        Cast in simple moulds, it symbolised status and access to rare materials,
        as well as early innovation in toolmaking.


        Shabti of Psamtik


        Replica
        of a Late Period Egyptian shabti (c. 600 BCE) made of vivid blue composition.
        With mummiform body, divine beard, and farm tools, it was inscribed to serve
        Psamtik in the afterlife. A symbol of resurrection, magical labour, and eternal
        service.'
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 4882262320171367339, guid: c480ee079c800aa42a2a66683d2783ad, type: 3}
